# capture fixture for the offline replay harness: packets + hand-transcribed P lines
#
# Second view on daikin_e_doc_packets.log: the same four R packets, plus the P1P2/P
# lines that belong to them, written BY HAND from the protocol tables. Nothing in this
# file is a recording - it only exists so that --against-capture has something to
# compare against in CI, without committing anything from the house.
#
# No recordings: every packet below is copied verbatim from upstream documentation,
# written in the four-field line format that tools/capture.sh produces (see
# captures/README.md):
#   <YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS> <retained 0|1> <topic> <payload>
#
# Sources
#   doc/P1P2Monitor-commands.md                          "Serial output from P1P2Monitor"
#   doc/LogicalFormat/Daikin-protocol-EHYHBX08AAV3.md    packet type 0x10 tables
# plus one packet assembled by hand (packet 4, see its comment).
#
# The R payloads are written the way this bridge republishes a bus packet on P1P2/R:
# "R", the 20 characters the ESP inserts from its own clock, then the rest of the
# ATmega line: " T  0.105: <hex>" for a bus packet, " P         <hex>" for a pseudo
# packet.
#
# Byte numbers below are payload bytes as numbered in the EHYHBX08AAV3 protocol doc,
# counting from 0 at the first byte after the 3-byte header (src, dst, type).
# Hand-checked expectations: daikin_e_doc_packets.E_SERIES.expect (shared with the
# first fixture). The golden file is shared too - same packets, so the same messages
# are expected: test/golden/daikin_e_doc_packets.E_SERIES.golden.txt.

# 1. 000010 request, main controller -> heat pump. Payload:
#      00 01 01 00 00 00 00 14 00 00 00 00 08 00 00 0F 00 00 3D 00   CRC 29
#    byte 0 bit 0 = 0      heat pump off
#    bytes 7-8 = 14 00     room heating setpoint = 20.0 C
#    bytes 15-16 = 0F 00   room cooling setpoint = 15.0 C
#    byte 18 = 3D          DHW setpoint = 61.0 C
2026-11-14T20:31:12 0 P1P2/R/P1P2MQTT/bridge0 R 2026-11-14 20:31:12 T  0.105: 0000100001010000000014000000000800000F00003D0029

# 2. 400010 response, heat pump -> main controller. Payload:
#      00 00 81 01 3D 00 0F 00 14 00 1A 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00   CRC E0
#    byte 2 bit 0 = 1  heating on            bit 1 = 0  cooling off
#    byte 2 bit 5 = 0  main zone off         bit 7 = 1  DHW tank valve
#    bytes 12-14 = 00 00 00   no error
#    byte 18 bit 0 = 0  compressor off
2026-11-14T20:31:12 0 P1P2/R/P1P2MQTT/bridge0 R 2026-11-14 20:31:12 T  0.024: 400010000081013D000F0014001A000000000000000000E0

# 3. pseudo packets - the two hex strings are copied verbatim from the example block in
#    doc/P1P2Monitor-commands.md:
#      P P         00000D0000000000000000000000000000000000000000C4
#      R P         40000D0D00000001C63D0000000000000000000000000019
#    They are written here in the R-topic form, because that is what a capture holds;
#    the "P P" prefix of the first documented line is not one of the line kinds this
#    bridge forwards (R/E/C/c/*), so of that line only the hex is used. The "P" marker
#    instead of a relative timestamp is how the ATmega marks pseudo packets, so the
#    harness must not try to read a timestamp there.
#    What these two packets show: 00000D is a counter/settings request, and 40000D
#    (src 0x40) is an answer to it. The E-series table has an explicit branch for that
#    source on type 0x0D (P1P2_ParameterConversion.h, `case 0x0D` -> `case 0x40`), which
#    decodes it into the bridge's pseudo-system keys: feeding it publishes C/9/ keys such
#    as Heating_Cooling_Auto, Number_Of_Zones and the four Preset_* values. The numbers
#    in the golden file are what the current code derives from the doc's example payload
#    - that payload is illustrative bytes from P1P2Monitor's own output, so the values are
#    pinned to detect changes, not asserted to be sensible readings.
2026-11-14T20:31:12 0 P1P2/R/P1P2MQTT/bridge0 R 2026-11-14 20:31:12 P         00000D0000000000000000000000000000000000000000C4
2026-11-14T20:31:12 0 P1P2/R/P1P2MQTT/bridge0 R 2026-11-14 20:31:12 P         40000D0D00000001C63D0000000000000000000000000019

# 4. assembled by hand, not from any doc: the same 000010 request with only byte 7
#    changed, 14 -> 15, so the room heating setpoint goes 20.0 -> 21.0 C. Every other
#    payload byte is unchanged and the CRC is recomputed with the firmware's own
#    algorithm (CRC-8, polynomial 0xD9 reflected, feed 0x00, over the 23 preceding
#    bytes). That algorithm was verified by reproducing the CRCs of the three documented
#    packets above exactly.
#    Expectation: exactly one parameter message - Room_Heating_Setpoint 21.0 - because
#    the decoder publishes on change only. Asserted in the .expect file.
2026-11-14T20:31:13 0 P1P2/R/P1P2MQTT/bridge0 R 2026-11-14 20:31:13 T  0.106: 0000100001010000000015000000000800000F00003D00C6

# --- the same window on the P1P2/P topic: hand-transcribed, not recorded ----------
# For each key below, the value is derived by hand from the payload bytes and the
# packet type 0x10 tables in doc/LogicalFormat/Daikin-protocol-EHYHBX08AAV3.md - the
# same derivation as in daikin_e_doc_packets.E_SERIES.expect, written here in capture
# format. This is a second, independent expression of that expectation, not a
# measurement: no bridge or broker was involved.
2026-11-14T20:31:12 0 P1P2/P/P1P2MQTT/bridge0/S/0/Altherma_On 0
2026-11-14T20:31:12 0 P1P2/P/P1P2MQTT/bridge0/S/0/Room_Heating_Setpoint 20.0
2026-11-14T20:31:12 0 P1P2/P/P1P2MQTT/bridge0/S/0/Room_Cooling_Setpoint 15.0
2026-11-14T20:31:12 0 P1P2/P/P1P2MQTT/bridge0/S/0/DHW_Setpoint 61.0
2026-11-14T20:31:12 0 P1P2/P/P1P2MQTT/bridge0/S/0/Quiet_Level 0
2026-11-14T20:31:12 0 P1P2/P/P1P2MQTT/bridge0/S/0/Climate_HC_Auto 0
2026-11-14T20:31:12 0 P1P2/P/P1P2MQTT/bridge0/S/1/Climate_Heating 1
2026-11-14T20:31:12 0 P1P2/P/P1P2MQTT/bridge0/S/1/Climate_Cooling 0
2026-11-14T20:31:12 0 P1P2/P/P1P2MQTT/bridge0/S/1/Valve_Zone_Main 0
2026-11-14T20:31:12 0 P1P2/P/P1P2MQTT/bridge0/S/1/Valve_DHW_Tank 1
2026-11-14T20:31:12 0 P1P2/P/P1P2MQTT/bridge0/M/1/ErrorCode1 0x00
2026-11-14T20:31:12 0 P1P2/P/P1P2MQTT/bridge0/M/1/ErrorCode2 0x00
2026-11-14T20:31:12 0 P1P2/P/P1P2MQTT/bridge0/M/1/ErrorSubCode 0x00
2026-11-14T20:31:12 0 P1P2/P/P1P2MQTT/bridge0/S/1/Compressor 0
# the byte 7 change (14 -> 15) is the only value that moves in this window
2026-11-14T20:31:13 0 P1P2/P/P1P2MQTT/bridge0/S/0/Room_Heating_Setpoint 21.0
